From dff9b2deb02a96e4320e0e86c4ac18f7fdde6f92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 331/488] soh: name the 12 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_gb.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 12 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Gb/z_en_gb.c; updating their references touches 3 files in total.

  * func_80A2F180 -> EnGb_UpdateTextId
    deduced, confidence HIGH: picks the Poe collector's greeting depending
    on whether the player has spoken to him before.

  * func_80A2F608 -> EnGb_UpdateColliders
    deduced, confidence HIGH: places the body collider 25 units in front of
    the actor and each bottle collider at its own offset, all rotated into
    the actor's frame.

  * func_80A2F760 -> EnGb_AreSoulsStirring
    deduced, confidence HIGH: returns whether any of the caged souls is
    currently in its stirred-up state, which suppresses the idle timer.

  * func_80A2F7C0 -> EnGb_SetupSwingStick
    deduced, confidence HIGH: starts the stick-swinging animation with its
    magic sfx and installs the swinging action.

  * func_80A2F83C -> EnGb_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the resting action: counts down to the next
    stick swing, offers the Poe exchange within 100 units, and routes an
    accepted trade to the ordinary, small-Poe or big-Poe reply.

  * func_80A2F94C -> EnGb_Talk
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the plain greeting, records that the
    player has spoken to him and returns to the idle.

  * func_80A2F9C0 -> EnGb_BuyPoe
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the small-Poe purchase reply; it records the
    conversation and returns to the idle.

  * func_80A2FA50 -> EnGb_BuyBigPoe
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the big-Poe purchase: empties the bottle, pays
    50 rupees, adds 100 Poe points and, at exactly 1000, moves on to the
    bottle reward instead of returning to the idle.

  * func_80A2FB40 -> EnGb_OfferBottle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: once the reward line is advanced it offers
    GI_BOTTLE.

  * func_80A2FBB0 -> EnGb_GiveBottle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: re-offers the bottle until the player takes
    it.

  * func_80A2FC0C -> EnGb_FinishGiveBottle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out the get-item textbox, refreshes the
    greeting and returns to the idle.

  * func_80A2FC70 -> EnGb_SwingStick
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the stick swing: on frame 18 it stirs all
    four caged souls, plays the wood-hit sfx and rearms the idle timer, and
    at the end returns to the looping idle animation.

